From 57ea143e7de728706f6fb37f11056d8b1b32d564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:55:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 94/94] drm/msm/gpu: Remove the bus vote when the GPU is
 suspended

disable_clk() parks the core clock with dev_pm_opp_set_rate(27 MHz),
which selects one of the lowest OPPs. When the OPP table carries
bandwidth (opp-peak-kBps, as on SDM630/SDM660), that also votes the
OPP's bandwidth on the GPU's memory path, and nothing removes it until
the GPU resumes. On SDM660 the path is tagged RPM_ALWAYS_TAG, so a
runtime-suspended GPU keeps asking the RPM for 1.2 GB/s of DDR
bandwidth, in the sleep set too, which keeps the BIMC clocked and the
SoC out of XO shutdown and VDD minimization.

Remove the vote the way the GMU and GMU wrapper paths already do, with
dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL). That also drops the required-opps of the
parked OPP. The next dev_pm_opp_set_rate() on resume finds the table
disabled and programs bandwidth and required-opps again.

Downstream does the same: KGSL's _slumber() goes through
kgsl_pwrctrl_disable() and kgsl_pwrctrl_axi(OFF) to
kgsl_pwrctrl_buslevel_update(false), which votes bus level 0 (0 KBps in
the RS6's grp3d bus table) and 0 to the GPU bandwidth devfreq.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
index ae6bf627c..c05537faf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -83,6 +83,13 @@ static int disable_clk(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 	if (gpu->rbbmtimer_clk)
 		clk_set_rate(gpu->rbbmtimer_clk, 0);
 
+	/*
+	 * Remove the bus vote. Parking the clock leaves an OPP selected, and
+	 * with it that OPP's bandwidth on the GPU's memory path, which would
+	 * keep DDR up for as long as the GPU is off.
+	 */
+	dev_pm_opp_set_opp(&gpu->pdev->dev, NULL);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
